-I'll pay ya.

260
00:08:49,663 --> 00:08:50,897
Come on, pick mine.

261
00:08:50,930 --> 00:08:53,733
NARRATOR: The judge feels the
weight and shape of the ears.

262
00:08:53,767 --> 00:08:55,970
-It's all done behind
protective chicken wire.

263
00:08:56,003 --> 00:08:59,440
NARRATOR: Then, he looks at the
evenness of the rows of grain--

264
00:08:59,473 --> 00:09:00,507
-Yes.

265
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,108
NARRATOR: --and the size
and shape of the kernels.

266
00:09:02,142 --> 00:09:03,110
-Oh my, yes.

267
00:09:03,143 --> 00:09:04,343
Yes, nice, oh.

268
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:06,480
NARRATOR: But surely none of
the corn is quite as fine as Mr.

269
00:09:06,513 --> 00:09:07,480
Olson's.

270
00:09:07,513 --> 00:09:08,950
-Don't tell your mother
we've been here, son.

271
00:09:08,983 --> 00:09:10,183
NARRATOR: It's time for lunch.

272
00:09:10,217 --> 00:09:13,487
-Let's go eat something great.

273
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:15,623
NARRATOR: Most of the
visitors at the fair

274
00:09:15,657 --> 00:09:18,192
have a quick bite at
one of the lunch stands.

275
00:09:18,225 --> 00:09:19,260
-I'm lost.

276
00:09:19,293 --> 00:09:20,260
Mother!

277
00:09:20,293 --> 00:09:22,330
NARRATOR: And my
foot-long hot dog

278
00:09:22,363 --> 00:09:23,830
looks mighty good to these boys.

279
00:09:23,863 --> 00:09:24,865
-Watch the boy on the left.

280
00:09:24,898 --> 00:09:27,100
His heart's about to explode!

281
00:09:27,133 --> 00:09:28,235
Wait!

282
00:09:28,268 --> 00:09:30,237
NARRATOR: But here at
the 4-H club camp--

283
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:31,237
-Is good, ya?

284
00:09:31,270 --> 00:09:32,973
NARRATOR: --where many
of the farm boys eat,

285
00:09:33,007 --> 00:09:35,542
they get fried chicken
with all the trimmings.

286
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:36,243
-What, tinsel?

287
00:09:36,277 --> 00:09:37,143
Little lights?

288
00:09:37,177 --> 00:09:40,948
-This is an actual
4-H feeding frenzy!

289
00:09:40,982 --> 00:09:43,483
NARRATOR: Other fairgoers
like to picnic on the grass,

290
00:09:43,517 --> 00:09:44,617
like this.

291
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:48,255
-Grazing in the grass is a
gas, baby, can you dig it?

292
00:09:48,288 --> 00:09:49,823
-Next up, freaks of nature!

293
00:09:49,857 --> 00:09:52,427
NARRATOR: Bob still
has lots to see.

294
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:53,927
This is a jet plane.

295
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:54,927
-Where's the corn go?

296
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,997
NARRATOR: Wonder what it
would be like to fly it?

297
00:09:57,030 --> 00:09:58,932
-Over Cambodia,
secretly maintaining

298
00:09:58,965 --> 00:10:00,067
plausible deniability.

299
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,968
NARRATOR: Here is a tractor.

300
00:10:02,002 --> 00:10:04,138
It's much like the
one Bob's father has.

301
00:10:04,172 --> 00:10:07,742
-Except this one doesn't have
father's arm stuck in it.

302
00:10:07,775 --> 00:10:09,443
NARRATOR: He knows how
to drive this all right.

303
00:10:09,477 --> 00:10:11,845
-OK, I'm a half a mile to the
interstate and I'm outta here!

304
00:10:11,878 --> 00:10:13,980
NARRATOR: Say,
listen to the band.

305
00:10:14,013 --> 00:10:15,817
It's time for the parade!

306
00:10:15,850 --> 00:10:19,487
-It's the Girl Corps, 100
magnificently trained girls!

307
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:22,957
-(SINGING IN HIGH VOICE) Here
we are now, entertain us.

308
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:25,458
I feel stupid, and contagious.

309
00:10:31,265 --> 00:10:34,868
-Admiral Halsey joins the fun.

310
00:10:34,902 --> 00:10:38,005
The family of shame.

311
00:10:38,038 --> 00:10:40,107
Captured pilots are paraded
before the citizens.

312
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,910
-Women are excited by
seeing the word "member."

313
00:10:42,943 --> 00:10:44,478
-(IN HIGH VOICE) Oh, my!

314
00:10:44,512 --> 00:10:46,813
NARRATOR: The parade is put
on by the farmers' clubs

315
00:10:46,847 --> 00:10:48,015
from all over the state.

316
00:10:48,048 --> 00:10:50,183
-Scientists aren't sure
what this represents.

317
00:10:50,217 --> 00:10:52,887
NARRATOR: This float was made
up by one of the 4-H clubs.

318
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:55,890
-In about two minutes.

319
00:10:55,923 --> 00:10:58,058
NARRATOR: Now at the grandstand,
the races are beginning.

320
00:10:58,092 --> 00:10:59,660
-Get the car, there's
carrots in the car!

321
00:10:59,693 --> 00:11:00,093
-Carrots?

322
00:11:00,127 --> 00:11:01,328
I love carrots.

323
00:11:01,362 --> 00:11:03,397
NARRATOR: And here come the
racers down the track and away.

324
00:11:03,430 --> 00:11:06,100
-A wheel slices into the
crowd, killing three.

325
00:11:06,133 --> 00:11:07,100
-Aiyee!

326
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:10,838
-Still, nothing measures
up to those bats, huh?

327
00:11:10,872 --> 00:11:13,407
NARRATOR: Here they come,
up the back stretch.

328
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,375
-I gotta go, I gotta
go, I really gotta go.

329
00:11:15,408 --> 00:11:17,812
NARRATOR: And Bob gets
there just in time.

330
00:11:17,845 --> 00:11:18,678
They're into the curve.

331
00:11:18,712 --> 00:11:20,782
-And they're into jazz.

332
00:11:20,815 --> 00:11:22,215
-Come on, you trunk of dog food!

333
00:11:22,248 --> 00:11:23,883
I've got a year's
allowance on ya!

334
00:11:23,917 --> 00:11:27,120
NARRATOR: They're going
into the home stretch.

335
00:11:27,153 --> 00:11:29,257
-Oh, hey guys, wait up.

336
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:31,458
NARRATOR: And here they
come across the finish.

337
00:11:31,492 --> 00:11:33,127
The race is over.

338
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:35,395
-And the Oak Ridge
Boys take the stage.

339
00:11:35,428 --> 00:11:39,567
-[Mumbled_singing]

340
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,835
-Dad, I owe Big Lenny 42 large.

341
00:11:41,868 --> 00:11:44,572
NARRATOR: Now it's
time for the calf show.

342
00:11:44,605 --> 00:11:47,442
Bob and Johnny are putting
the finishing touches

343
00:11:47,475 --> 00:11:48,275
on their calves.

344
00:11:48,308 --> 00:11:49,577
-Adding hooker
headers and decals.

345
00:11:49,610 --> 00:11:51,378
NARRATOR: Johnny
polishes up the horns--

346
00:11:51,412 --> 00:11:53,447
-[making_squeaking_noises]

347
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,950
NARRATOR: And father,
of course, stands by.

348
00:11:55,983 --> 00:11:57,685
-Doing nothing.

349
00:11:57,718 --> 00:11:59,487
NARRATOR: Now the
boys take their calves

350
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,822
to the arena, where
the show is beginning.

351
00:12:01,855 --> 00:12:03,757
-First is the evening
gown competition.

352
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:06,093
-We have some tape of the
cows playing on the beach

353
00:12:06,127 --> 00:12:07,695
earlier this week.

354
00:12:07,728 --> 00:12:10,230
NARRATOR: Into the
big, shadowy arena,

355
00:12:10,263 --> 00:12:13,600
many other boys and girls
are leading their calves.

356
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:14,535
Here come Bob and Johnny.

357
00:12:14,568 --> 00:12:15,035
-What?

358
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:17,103
I'm not sweating.

359
00:12:17,137 --> 00:12:19,240
NARRATOR: They take their
places in a long line.

360
00:12:19,273 --> 00:12:20,107
-What losers!

361
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:21,408
NARRATOR: And the
judge is to choose

362
00:12:21,442 --> 00:12:24,445
which among all these
calves is the best.

363
00:12:24,478 --> 00:12:26,113
-But all the calves
are winners, really.

364
00:12:26,147 --> 00:12:27,815
It's just great that
they got involved!

365
00:12:27,848 --> 00:12:30,350
NARRATOR: Bob and Johnny
hope he'll choose theirs.

366
00:12:30,383 --> 00:12:30,883
-Whoop!

367
00:12:30,917 --> 00:12:32,787
Hey, that's my scar.

368
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:34,422
NARRATOR: Up here, the
folks are looking on.

369
00:12:34,455 --> 00:12:36,223
-Let's get busy
in the car, honey.

370
00:12:36,257 --> 00:12:39,160
NARRATOR: Now the judge
is coming down the line.

371
00:12:39,193 --> 00:12:42,663
He looks at each calf
closely with a practiced eye,

372
00:12:42,697 --> 00:12:45,532
and quickly sees the best
and the weakest point.

373
00:12:45,565 --> 00:12:47,167
-He is all-knowing and wise.

374
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:49,002
NARRATOR: Now he orders
the doubtful calves out

375
00:12:49,035 --> 00:12:49,902
of the show.

376
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:51,938
-The Masked Avenger
cow is eliminated.

377
00:12:51,972 --> 00:12:53,573
-I hate these cattle calls.

378
00:12:53,607 --> 00:12:54,775
NARRATOR: Too bad.

379
00:12:54,808 --> 00:12:55,977
Bob loses out.

380
00:12:56,010 --> 00:12:56,877
-Bob hates himself.

381
00:12:56,910 --> 00:12:59,947
NARRATOR: But what about Johnny?

382
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,080
He's still in line.

383
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:04,117
And now the judge wants to
see his calf in the open.

384
00:13:04,150 --> 00:13:07,522
-He realizes he had not
known cow until this day.

385
00:13:07,555 --> 00:13:09,957
NARRATOR: He looks at
Johnny's calf very carefully.

386
00:13:09,990 --> 00:13:11,692
-He feels a stirring.

387
00:13:11,725 --> 00:13:12,760
NARRATOR: What's this?

388
00:13:12,793 --> 00:13:15,930
Here's Johnny back in line.

389
00:13:15,963 --> 00:13:18,098
Well, it looks like
he has a winner.

390
00:13:18,132 --> 00:13:19,233
-Men are fools, dear.

391
00:13:19,267 --> 00:13:20,133
Remember that.

392
00:13:20,167 --> 00:13:21,902
NARRATOR: Now the
judge is picking out

393
00:13:21,935 --> 00:13:23,137
the champion of them all.

394
00:13:23,170 --> 00:13:24,370
-I am the greatest!

395
00:13:24,403 --> 00:13:27,507
NARRATOR: It takes careful work
to choose the calf with just

396
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:31,245
the right size, and build,
and weight, and firmness.

397
00:13:31,278 --> 00:13:33,580
-And overall panache!

398
00:13:33,613 --> 00:13:36,817
NARRATOR: One by one, the
judge ranks the calves

399
00:13:36,850 --> 00:13:39,520
and sends them back to their
proper places in the line.

400
00:13:39,553 --> 00:13:41,788
-Life goes on, dull as before.

401
00:13:41,822 --> 00:13:44,023
NARRATOR: At last,
the choice is made.

402
00:13:44,057 --> 00:13:45,092
-But he won't tell anyone!

403
00:13:45,125 --> 00:13:47,393
It's so frustrating.

404
00:13:47,427 --> 00:13:48,695
NARRATOR: The
judge's work is done.

405
00:13:48,728 --> 00:13:50,097
He has picked the winners.

406
00:13:50,130 --> 00:13:52,498
-Quite a coup, getting
Clarence Darrow to judge.

407
00:13:52,532 --> 00:13:53,767
-And the crowd goes wild.

408
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,000
-(DULLY) Yay.

409
00:13:55,033 --> 00:13:57,905
NARRATOR: Well, the champion's
blue ribbon goes to a girl.

410
00:13:57,938 --> 00:13:59,907
-The cows are furious!

411
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:01,342
NARRATOR: Johnny
gets a ribbon, too.

412
00:14:01,375 --> 00:14:02,142
-Yeah, thanks.

413
00:14:02,175 --> 00:14:03,177
NARRATOR: His calf is a winner.

414
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:04,812
-Oh, look at this, I
got a stinkin' ribbon.

415
00:14:07,648 --> 00:14:11,052
NARRATOR: Now the day's work
is over, and it's time for fun.

416
00:14:11,085 --> 00:14:12,687
-So they leave the fair.

417
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:13,987
NARRATOR: The
gates to the midway

418
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:16,523
open on 100 ways of having fun.

419
00:14:16,557 --> 00:14:18,225
-Or you can just get hammered.

420
00:14:18,258 --> 00:14:21,895
NARRATOR: There are shows
and games of every kind.

421
00:14:21,928 --> 00:14:26,633
And, best of all, a thrilling
ride on the giant Ferris wheel.

422
00:14:26,667 --> 00:14:28,402
-It's the Man in
the Hat exhibit!

423
00:14:28,435 --> 00:14:30,203
-Musty carnies,
drunk by 10:00 AM!

424
00:14:32,773 --> 00:14:35,442
NARRATOR: Here they go,
quickly into the seat,

425
00:14:35,475 --> 00:14:39,447
with the bar fastened tight
to keep them in safely.

426
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,380
-Goodbye, Susan.

427
00:14:40,413 --> 00:14:41,948
If anything should
happen, I love you.

428
00:14:41,982 --> 00:14:43,117
I love you too, Petey.

429
00:14:43,150 --> 00:14:45,987
NARRATOR: And now
the wheel turns.

430
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:48,722
Up, up, high in the air.

431
00:14:48,755 --> 00:14:51,492
And this is how it seems to
ride the big Ferris wheel.

432
00:14:51,525 --> 00:14:53,027
-It's this disappointing.

433
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:54,928
-The director got Artie here!

434
00:14:54,962 --> 00:14:56,530
-(SINGING) Love roller coaster!

435
00:14:56,563 --> 00:14:58,932
-Well, Ferris wheel.

436
00:14:58,965 --> 00:15:01,235
NARRATOR: And now for
a ride on The Whip.

437
00:15:01,268 --> 00:15:02,368
-[Vomiting_sounds]

438
00:15:02,402 --> 00:15:05,405
NARRATOR: This is how it
seems to ride on the swooping,

439
00:15:05,438 --> 00:15:06,373
whirling Whip.

440
00:15:06,407 --> 00:15:08,342
-This is how it seems
to be thrown clear

441
00:15:08,375 --> 00:15:10,343
as the cables snap.

442
00:15:10,377 --> 00:15:12,578
NARRATOR: Too soon,
the rides are over.

443
00:15:12,612 --> 00:15:15,615
-The lawsuits begin.

444
00:15:15,648 --> 00:15:19,285
NARRATOR: And too soon, all
the fun comes to an end.

445
00:15:19,318 --> 00:15:20,218
-[Singing_incomprehensibly]

446
00:15:20,252 --> 00:15:22,923
NARRATOR: But our
friends are very happy.

447
00:15:22,957 --> 00:15:25,225
They've had a wonderful
day at the fair.

448
00:15:25,258 --> 00:15:26,227
-You spent your nickel!

449
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:27,260
We're done!

450
00:15:35,702 --> 00:15:36,335
-Ah!

451
00:15:36,368 --> 00:15:38,172
Tonight on Generic TV Movie.

452
00:15:38,205 --> 00:15:42,208
[Theme music playing]

453
00:15:42,242 --> 00:15:45,445
-Hey, watch out for my bike!

454
00:15:45,478 --> 00:15:47,080
-Hey, I cracked their code.

455
00:15:47,113 --> 00:15:49,917
I'm pretty sure it's
called "Diamond Head."

456
00:15:49,950 --> 00:15:54,153
-Code Name-- Cubic
Zirconium Head.

457
00:15:54,187 --> 00:15:57,457
-Quinn Martin considered
this is most personal film.

458
00:15:57,490 --> 00:16:01,462
-Mm, father what a waste.

459
00:16:01,495 --> 00:16:03,063
-Is he our action hero?

460
00:16:03,097 --> 00:16:04,532
-I want to see Don Ho!

461
00:16:15,508 --> 00:16:18,278
-Ward, dear, would you see
what little Elvis is up to?

462
00:16:22,015 --> 00:16:25,052
-Ah, a little Maui Wowie
to start things off.

463
00:16:25,085 --> 00:16:26,353
-Hey, that's no priest!

464
00:16:26,387 --> 00:16:28,888
That's Lovejoy!

465
00:16:28,922 --> 00:16:35,662
-Rosie O'Donnell
in "The Gauntlet."

466
00:16:35,695 --> 00:16:37,497
-I want a picture of Lovejoy.

467
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:40,133
-Susan, you sit next to Lovejoy.

468
00:16:40,167 --> 00:16:42,468
-Martin Short.

469
00:16:42,502 --> 00:16:44,672
-I see my latest exhibit
meets with your approval.

470
00:16:47,273 --> 00:16:51,178
-Apparently Jack Lorde doesn't
even like it here, huh?

471
00:16:51,212 --> 00:16:54,448
-Taking a Greyhound to
Hawaii wasn't a good idea.

472
00:16:54,482 --> 00:16:55,415
-Ah, Mr. Jesus.

473
00:16:55,448 --> 00:16:58,118
You have a nasty
habit of surviving.

474
00:16:58,152 --> 00:16:58,752
-That's mine.

475
00:16:58,785 --> 00:16:59,753
I think that's mine.

476
00:16:59,787 --> 00:17:00,187
-That one?

477
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:01,053
-Yeah.

478
00:17:01,087 --> 00:17:03,123
-Ah, the gripping
luggage sequence.

479
00:17:03,157 --> 00:17:04,825
I'm not going to tell
you what happens.

480
00:17:04,858 --> 00:17:06,927
I'm just going to say--
someone's luggage gets lost!

481
00:17:10,197 --> 00:17:11,932
-Ah, Mr. Handbag.

482
00:17:11,965 --> 00:17:15,868
Once again, I see that you
are not on the carousel yet.

483
00:17:15,902 --> 00:17:19,440
-They'd better not lose my
Saint Peter's finger bone.

484
00:17:19,473 --> 00:17:23,377
-He looks like he just
got out of gym class.

485
00:17:23,410 --> 00:17:24,645
-That guy's a sinner.

486
00:17:24,678 --> 00:17:25,912
They're all sinners.

487
00:17:25,945 --> 00:17:27,513
CUSTOMS OFFICER (OFFSCREEN):
Anything to declare?

488
00:17:27,547 --> 00:17:28,480
-I declare my genius!

489
00:17:28,513 --> 00:17:29,883
CUSTOMS OFFICER
(OFFSCREEN): Thank you, sir.

490
00:17:29,917 --> 00:17:30,850
-Hey, that guy!

491
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:31,785
What was he in?

492
00:17:31,818 --> 00:17:32,285
-Yeah!

493
00:17:32,318 --> 00:17:34,187
Uh, um.

494
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:37,223
-Was that guy in?

495
00:17:37,257 --> 00:17:38,292
-Well, hello.

496
00:17:38,325 --> 00:17:39,627
Nomine Patris.

497
00:17:39,660 --> 00:17:41,728
Heh.

498
00:17:41,762 --> 00:17:43,230
-Anything to declare, sir?

499
00:17:43,263 --> 00:17:43,830
-I'm Lovejoy.

500
00:17:43,863 --> 00:17:44,763
Oops!

501
00:17:44,797 --> 00:17:46,433
-Not unless you wish
to make a donation.

502
00:17:46,467 --> 00:17:48,835
I'm on a fundraising tour
of your lovely island.

503
00:17:48,868 --> 00:17:49,368
-Yeah.

504
00:17:49,402 --> 00:17:50,337
Anything to declare?

505
00:17:50,370 --> 00:17:51,905
-Maybe next time.

506
00:17:51,938 --> 00:17:52,807
Good luck.

507
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:53,673
-Thank you.

508
00:17:53,707 --> 00:17:55,742
-Kisses!

509
00:17:55,775 --> 00:17:57,912
-Enjoy the cocaine, father!

510
00:17:57,945 --> 00:18:01,080
LOUDSPEAKER: Luggage
for flight 05, Chicago--

511
00:18:01,113 --> 00:18:02,782
-Take over for me, will you?

512
00:18:02,815 --> 00:18:05,785
