00:36:02,728 --> 00:36:03,695
-Commander.

1039
00:36:03,728 --> 00:36:04,763
I always enjoy a vacation
from the Pentagon.

1040
00:36:04,797 --> 00:36:06,132
-Professor En-Ping
from the University--

1041
00:36:06,165 --> 00:36:07,098
-Peew!

1042
00:36:07,132 --> 00:36:08,233
-Professor, I hear you
and your colleagues

1043
00:36:08,267 --> 00:36:10,737
have got some surprises
for us up in Makapu'u.

1044
00:36:10,770 --> 00:36:12,372
-From what they tell me.

1045
00:36:12,405 --> 00:36:15,708
I hope we're the last
men on Earth to see it.

1046
00:36:15,742 --> 00:36:16,242
-Hey!

1047
00:36:16,275 --> 00:36:17,777
This is a TV movie!

1048
00:36:17,810 --> 00:36:18,777
Rip off!

1049
00:36:18,810 --> 00:36:19,312
Boo.

1050
00:36:22,915 --> 00:36:24,850
-You and your
chaperone will travel

1051
00:36:24,883 --> 00:36:27,052
to what is apparently Hawaii!

1052
00:36:27,085 --> 00:36:29,422
-Oliver Twist had more Hawaiian
locations than this movie.

1053
00:36:29,455 --> 00:36:32,057
-The Kentucky Cycle has
more Hawaii locations.

1054
00:36:34,727 --> 00:36:37,095
-Oh, the all-cat food store.

1055
00:36:37,128 --> 00:36:39,765
-Oh, I've got to pick up a can
of tampons for my girlfriend.

1056
00:36:42,802 --> 00:36:45,403
-Do you have any canned items?

1057
00:36:45,437 --> 00:36:48,373
-Across the street, room 205.

1058
00:36:48,407 --> 00:36:49,875
Interpol did the rest.

1059
00:36:49,908 --> 00:36:51,143
-Just looking, thanks.

1060
00:36:51,177 --> 00:36:54,880
-Hikaru Sakai, a street
kamikaze from Tokyo.

1061
00:36:54,913 --> 00:36:57,717
He's a professional assassin.

1062
00:36:57,750 --> 00:37:00,853
The other guy is Ernest
Graeber, once a contract hit man

1063
00:37:00,887 --> 00:37:02,087
for East German intelligence.

1064
00:37:02,120 --> 00:37:04,657
-Always a contract hit man
for East German intelligence.

1065
00:37:04,690 --> 00:37:06,058
-Calls Tahiti home now.

1066
00:37:06,092 --> 00:37:07,258
-Don't smell the bok choi.

1067
00:37:07,292 --> 00:37:08,995
-Very bad dudes.

1068
00:37:09,028 --> 00:37:09,662
-Where are they now?

1069
00:37:09,695 --> 00:37:10,763
-Staying with mom.

1070
00:37:10,797 --> 00:37:14,700
-Mama Chongs, eating steaks.

1071
00:37:14,733 --> 00:37:15,702
-Well, the three regular team.

1072
00:37:15,735 --> 00:37:18,203
-If they show up,
honk twice, huh?

1073
00:37:18,237 --> 00:37:19,138
-Yeah, sure.

1074
00:37:19,172 --> 00:37:19,938
-Hey, hey!

1075
00:37:19,972 --> 00:37:22,140
You've got to pay
for the Sheeva!

1076
00:37:22,173 --> 00:37:24,277
-Where in the hell did I park?

1077
00:37:24,310 --> 00:37:26,578
-Lot of goofing off in
the undercover business.

1078
00:37:29,548 --> 00:37:30,082
-Shout.

1079
00:37:30,115 --> 00:37:31,217
Shout.

1080
00:37:31,250 --> 00:37:34,487
Let it all out!

1081
00:37:34,520 --> 00:37:36,588
-The Eiger Sanction had
more Hawaiian locations

1082
00:37:36,622 --> 00:37:37,890
than this movie.

1083
00:37:37,923 --> 00:37:40,192
It's the kookiest
surveillance ever!

1084
00:37:40,225 --> 00:37:42,495
Hoo-hoo!

1085
00:37:42,528 --> 00:37:45,063
-He promised Sid and
Nancy he'd stop by.

1086
00:37:50,135 --> 00:37:51,903
-He lives in Hawaii,
but somehow he

1087
00:37:51,937 --> 00:37:54,307
still has a furnished
room in St. Paul.

1088
00:37:58,143 --> 00:38:01,213
-I just have the urge
to clean this lock.

1089
00:38:01,247 --> 00:38:04,050
-Ooh, spidery hands.

1090
00:38:04,083 --> 00:38:05,550
-Gollum breaks
into an apartment.

1091
00:38:08,853 --> 00:38:10,757
[Muffled]

1092
00:38:10,790 --> 00:38:12,858
-Ah, now the payoff.

1093
00:38:12,892 --> 00:38:13,825
Ah hah!

1094
00:38:16,628 --> 00:38:17,863
-Ergon Cable!

1095
00:38:17,897 --> 00:38:19,665
-Just here to drill through
your hardwood floors.

1096
00:38:23,002 --> 00:38:26,772
-Wow, that's a big-ass phone.

1097
00:38:26,805 --> 00:38:28,607
-This looks like
Daddy-O's apartments.

1098
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:31,277
Except for the big-ass phone.

1099
00:38:31,310 --> 00:38:33,878
-Forget it, no way.

1100
00:38:33,912 --> 00:38:36,948
There's not a natural
fiber on that man.

1101
00:38:36,982 --> 00:38:38,750
-Maybe I'm gonna call
Sydney-- Australia!

1102
00:38:45,357 --> 00:38:50,295
-Take one of these now, and
take one after every phone call.

1103
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:54,167
It doesn't do anything, but at
least he knows it's in there.

1104
00:38:54,200 --> 00:38:56,302
-This is the movie
poster right there!

1105
00:38:56,335 --> 00:38:56,935
Sold millions.

1106
00:39:01,773 --> 00:39:04,008
-Isn't that that guy
who was on that show?

1107
00:39:04,042 --> 00:39:04,777
What's those shows?

1108
00:39:07,447 --> 00:39:10,515
-Sort of a Cannon-y "McMillan
and Wife" type of thing?

1109
00:39:10,548 --> 00:39:15,620
-Rope had more Hawaiian
locations than this film!

1110
00:39:15,653 --> 00:39:18,857
He's wearing Mary
Tyler Moor's pantsuit.

1111
00:39:18,890 --> 00:39:20,592
-Well, he wants the match there.

1112
00:39:20,625 --> 00:39:21,327
I'll put it back.

1113
00:39:21,360 --> 00:39:21,993
It's kind of weird.

1114
00:39:24,963 --> 00:39:26,132
-It's Shirley Hemphill!

1115
00:39:32,270 --> 00:39:33,972
-(SINGING) At Bene,
at Beneficial.

1116
00:39:40,345 --> 00:39:42,815
[Suspenseful music building]

1117
00:39:42,848 --> 00:39:43,348
-Whoooo!

1118
00:39:47,318 --> 00:39:48,787
-Whoooo!

1119
00:39:48,820 --> 00:39:49,788
-Oh, what am I going to do?

1120
00:39:49,822 --> 00:39:50,790
I'm uncool!

1121
00:39:54,260 --> 00:39:57,663
[Imitating suspenseful music]

1122
00:39:57,697 --> 00:40:00,065
-I put in a matchstick
and it's foolproof.

1123
00:40:00,098 --> 00:40:02,333
Saves on a costly alarm system.

1124
00:40:02,367 --> 00:40:04,837
-You smell high karate
something fierce.

1125
00:40:07,338 --> 00:40:09,275
-This thing is damp!

1126
00:40:11,877 --> 00:40:13,678
-Carmen Miranda's in there.

1127
00:40:16,448 --> 00:40:18,817
-Now back to the jaunty
Roy Thinnes theme!

1128
00:40:18,850 --> 00:40:20,652
-This is so almost Mitchell.

1129
00:40:20,685 --> 00:40:22,353
-It's about 50 pounds
short of Mitchell.

1130
00:40:26,858 --> 00:40:28,227
-So.

1131
00:40:28,260 --> 00:40:29,295
Any Bilakhia?

1132
00:40:29,328 --> 00:40:31,297
-Back to the
exciting tuna store!

1133
00:40:31,330 --> 00:40:32,565
-I planted a bug
where they'll be

1134
00:40:32,598 --> 00:40:35,033
sure to find it when they do
their move on Tree, I hope.

1135
00:40:35,067 --> 00:40:36,168
You stay with them, huh?

1136
00:40:36,202 --> 00:40:37,402
-Right.

1137
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:41,340
-And he's good at conveying
incomprehensible plot points.

1138
00:40:41,373 --> 00:40:44,643
-Well, it's been nice being
here in downtown Fargo,

1139
00:40:44,677 --> 00:40:46,078
but I should be
getting back to Hawaii.

1140
00:40:48,780 --> 00:40:52,283
-This is too nice a place for
a deadly game of cat and mouse.

1141
00:41:01,327 --> 00:41:02,862
-Aw, people got
to start buttoning

1142
00:41:02,895 --> 00:41:05,130
their shirts in this movie!

1143
00:41:05,163 --> 00:41:06,898
-Everything seems all right.

1144
00:41:06,932 --> 00:41:07,633
-Trust the matchstick.

1145
00:41:07,667 --> 00:41:09,468
-One thing is sure.

1146
00:41:09,502 --> 00:41:11,303
We had a visitor.

1147
00:41:11,337 --> 00:41:12,270
-Let's take this place apart.

1148
00:41:12,303 --> 00:41:16,108
-Let's put the ceiling
where the floor is.

1149
00:41:16,142 --> 00:41:18,043
-Daddy, let's get a
two-bedroom next time.

1150
00:41:18,077 --> 00:41:19,143
It's crowded in here.

1151
00:41:23,315 --> 00:41:24,683
-Are these your tap pants?

1152
00:41:28,287 --> 00:41:29,855
-I need to call Dad.

1153
00:41:29,888 --> 00:41:30,522
Been too long.

1154
00:41:34,827 --> 00:41:37,128
-Premature funk music.

1155
00:41:37,162 --> 00:41:39,063
-There's always been
a bug in here, right?

1156
00:41:39,097 --> 00:41:39,932
-Sakai.

1157
00:41:39,965 --> 00:41:40,465
-'S all right.

1158
00:41:43,435 --> 00:41:44,970
-There's a rattlesnake
in my phone!

1159
00:41:48,273 --> 00:41:49,742
-The new Cadillac
lease program--

1160
00:41:49,775 --> 00:42:00,987
a simple up-front
payment of $47,000.

1161
00:42:01,020 --> 00:42:03,522
-We can't have Van
Dykes in the Navy!

1162
00:42:03,555 --> 00:42:06,092
-It's the slacker Navy.

1163
00:42:06,125 --> 00:42:08,127
-See, I've written a lot
of checks to Davanni's.

1164
00:42:08,160 --> 00:42:09,193
-Go right in, sir.

1165
00:42:13,832 --> 00:42:16,402
-Got the Navy wrapped
around their fingers.

1166
00:42:16,435 --> 00:42:18,403
-Yeah, you jerks are
no better than me.

1167
00:42:18,437 --> 00:42:19,872
Glad I went through
boot camp for this.

1168
00:42:19,905 --> 00:42:21,273
Join the Navy and see the world!

1169
00:42:21,307 --> 00:42:22,573
Yeah, more like open gates!

1170
00:42:22,607 --> 00:42:23,675
-That's a security guard.

1171
00:42:23,708 --> 00:42:25,610
-Oh, sorry.

1172
00:42:25,643 --> 00:42:27,078
-Gee, they fenced
in the entire ocean.

1173
00:42:31,050 --> 00:42:33,085
-They're making a stop at
the lumber yard, I see!

1174
00:42:33,118 --> 00:42:34,987
-We need some
plywood and a thing

1175
00:42:35,020 --> 00:42:36,322
to roll the garden hose on.

1176
00:42:41,593 --> 00:42:42,895
-OK, do you have brunch?

1177
00:42:46,132 --> 00:42:48,733
-Why hello, Captain Stubing!

1178
00:42:48,767 --> 00:42:49,402
Merrill.

1179
00:42:49,435 --> 00:42:50,535
-Gentlemen.

1180
00:42:50,568 --> 00:42:52,270
You've already met
Professor En-Ping.

1181
00:42:52,303 --> 00:42:52,770
-Ping!

1182
00:42:52,803 --> 00:42:53,705
-Hello, Professor.

1183
00:42:53,738 --> 00:42:54,973
-Thank you, Sherman.

1184
00:42:55,007 --> 00:42:57,542
Dr. Yamamoto, this
is Colonel Butler.

1185
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:58,477
-Not Lovejoy.

1186
00:42:58,510 --> 00:42:59,243
-A pleasure.

1187
00:42:59,277 --> 00:43:00,178
-What's with your moustache?

1188
00:43:00,212 --> 00:43:01,547
-This isn't the
Pentagon, Colonel,

1189
00:43:01,580 --> 00:43:02,982
but I think you'll
find this interesting.

1190
00:43:03,015 --> 00:43:04,650
-Oh, I'm sure I will.

1191
00:43:04,683 --> 00:43:05,317
Shall we begin?

1192
00:43:05,350 --> 00:43:06,152
-The beguine?

1193
00:43:06,185 --> 00:43:06,685
Ha!

1194
00:43:06,718 --> 00:43:07,687
Little-- never mind.

1195
00:43:10,622 --> 00:43:11,957
-For security
reasons, we maintain

1196
00:43:11,990 --> 00:43:14,460
our experimental
laboratory below sea level.

1197
00:43:14,493 --> 00:43:17,095
-Sure you do.

1198
00:43:17,128 --> 00:43:22,133
-Our test began with a rare cone
snail called the cloth of gold.

1199
00:43:22,167 --> 00:43:23,502
-Holy cow are they
below sea level.

1200
00:43:23,535 --> 00:43:25,337
-On contact, its
microscopic needles

1201
00:43:25,370 --> 00:43:28,640
inject alkaloids, which paralyze
the central nervous system.

1202
00:43:28,673 --> 00:43:29,475
Instantaneous death.

1203
00:43:29,508 --> 00:43:31,177
-And it's so good with kids.

1204
00:43:31,210 --> 00:43:34,212
-We extracted the liquid
poison, vaporized it--

1205
00:43:34,245 --> 00:43:35,147
-Added some leather.

1206
00:43:38,850 --> 00:43:39,852
-The result was astounding.

1207
00:43:43,888 --> 00:43:47,158
[Theme music playing]

1208
00:43:49,662 --> 00:43:50,162
-Hey Mike!

1209
00:43:50,195 --> 00:43:50,828
-Mike!
-Hey Mike!

1210
00:43:50,862 --> 00:43:51,330
-Mike!

1211
00:43:51,363 --> 00:43:51,830
Mike!

1212
00:43:51,863 --> 00:43:52,563
-Hey Mike, Mike.

1213
00:43:52,597 --> 00:43:53,898
-Let's play some Litho-Fungo.

1214
00:43:53,932 --> 00:43:54,633
-Yeah, come on!

1215
00:43:54,667 --> 00:43:55,433
Come on, come on!

1216
00:43:55,467 --> 00:43:56,702
-I'd really like
to, guys, but I've

1217
00:43:56,735 --> 00:43:59,003
got to finish
alphabetizing my CDs.

1218
00:43:59,037 --> 00:43:59,872
I'll see ya.

1219
00:43:59,905 --> 00:44:00,305
-Pbb.

1220
00:44:00,338 --> 00:44:00,805
Huh.

1221
00:44:00,838 --> 00:44:01,772
-Jeez.

1222
00:44:01,805 --> 00:44:04,142
I'd like to suggest
that Mike is less than a

1223
00:44:04,175 --> 00:44:07,545
fulfilling roommate, but I'm
afraid Magic Voice will--

1224
00:44:07,578 --> 00:44:08,580
WOMAN'S VOICE: Thank you, Crow.

1225
00:44:08,613 --> 00:44:10,482
I'm not finished with you yet.

1226
00:44:10,515 --> 00:44:15,220
Let's see what it would be like
if you lived with, oh, say,

1227
00:44:15,253 --> 00:44:18,257
a Crash Test Dummy!

1228
00:44:18,290 --> 00:44:19,892
-Brad Roberts?

1229
00:44:19,925 --> 00:44:21,660
-[Mumbled_singing]

1230
00:44:21,693 --> 00:44:22,393
-That voice!

1231
00:44:22,427 --> 00:44:24,497
-[Mumbled_singing]

1232
00:44:24,530 --> 00:44:26,365
-It hurts!

1233
00:44:26,398 --> 00:44:34,305
-[Mumbled_singing]

1234
00:44:34,338 --> 00:44:35,340
-That was close.

1235
00:44:35,373 --> 00:44:37,175
-Point taken, Magic Voice.

1236
00:44:37,208 --> 00:44:37,808
-All right.

1237
00:44:37,842 --> 00:44:39,243
Got the CDs alphabetized.

1238
00:44:39,277 --> 00:44:40,178
Who's for Yahtzee?

1239
00:44:40,212 --> 00:44:42,147
-Oh yes, oh yes, oh yes!

1240
00:44:42,180 --> 00:44:44,750
WOMAN'S VOICE: Movie
sign in three seconds.

1241
00:44:44,783 --> 00:44:45,483
Ha ha!

1242
00:44:45,517 --> 00:44:46,118
Just kidding.

1243
00:44:46,152 --> 00:44:46,618
-Whew!

1244
00:44:46,652 --> 00:44:50,088
[Buzzing]

1245
00:45:02,733 --> 00:45:04,235
-[Sobbing]

1246
00:45:04,268 --> 00:45:05,470
-Don't let go!

1247
00:45:05,503 --> 00:45:05,970
-Come on!

1248
00:45:06,003 --> 00:45:06,472
-No.

1249
00:45:06,505 --> 00:45:07,405
No.

1250
00:45:07,438 --> 00:45:09,742
---with unlimited
killing potential.

1251
00:45:09,775 --> 00:45:11,777
-Amazing biochemical
breakthrough.

1252
00:45:11,810 --> 00:45:12,845
Incredible.

1253
00:45:12,878 --> 00:45:14,513
But you must stop these tests.

1254
00:45:14,547 --> 00:45:16,782
We outlawed chemical
warfare eight years ago.

1255
00:45:16,815 --> 00:45:19,383
How much of this gold
cross have you made?

1256
00:45:19,417 --> 00:45:20,050
-Lots!

1257
00:45:20,083 --> 00:45:20,818
---with the underwater test.

1258
00:45:20,852 --> 00:45:21,987
We've destroyed the rest.

1259
00:45:22,020 --> 00:45:24,557
-Normal precautionary
measures, Colonel.

1260
00:45:24,590 --> 00:45:27,492
We can't have these experiments
falling into strange hands.

1261
00:45:27,525 --> 00:45:27,993
Of course.

1262
00:45:28,027 --> 00:45:28,560
-Pssh.

1263
00:45:28,593 --> 00:45:30,362
Think I don't know that?

1264
00:45:30,395 --> 00:45:32,330
-May I see what
precautions you've taken?

1265
00:45:32,363 --> 00:45:34,533
-And top thinking
that I'm Lovejoy.

1266
00:45:34,567 --> 00:45:36,302
-We maintain two safety checks.

1267
00:45:36,335 --> 00:45:37,302
-And that's about it.

1268
00:45:37,335 --> 00:45:40,938
-The gas is locked in
this compression chamber

1269
00:45:40,972 --> 00:45:42,007
and kept under pressure.

1270
00:45:42,040 --> 00:45:46,077
-Then your class ring
is buffed and polished.

1271
00:45:46,110 --> 00:45:47,512
-Oh, that's no good.

1272
00:45:47,545 --> 00:45:48,313
That'll ruin a planet.

1273
00:45:48,347 --> 00:45:49,413
Ha ha!

1274
00:45:49,447 --> 00:45:51,350
-Additionally, the vial
itself is also pressurized.

1275
00:45:54,218 --> 00:45:57,322
-I mean, usually
it's pressurized.

1276
00:45:57,355 --> 00:46:00,058
-And we pay a high school
kid to keep an eye on it.

1277
00:46:02,760 --> 00:46:03,962
-And your research?

1278
00:46:03,995 --> 00:46:06,063
-Still got two weeks
before the report's due.

1279
00:46:06,097 --> 00:46:07,867
-It's all been
recorded on tapes.

1280
00:46:07,900 --> 00:46:10,502
Formulas, chemical
compounds, every step

1281
00:46:10,535 --> 00:46:12,603
of the test from
the very beginning,

1282
00:46:12,637 --> 00:46:14,540
including the exact
amounts of the mixture.

1283
00:46:14,573 --> 00:46:16,375
-Well, when do we see
the underwater test?

1284
00:46:16,408 --> 00:46:18,610
-Colonel, surely
you've seen enough.

1285
00:46:18,643 --> 00:46:20,845
-Commander, your report
mentioned two tests.

1286
00:46:20,878 --> 00:46:22,813
Until I see both
of them, I'm not

1287
00:46:22,847 --> 00:46:25,717
authorized to give
a final judgement.

1288
00:46:25,750 --> 00:46:27,085
-I hate you.

1289
00:46:27,118 --> 00:46:29,153
-Very well, Colonel.

1290
00:46:29,187 --> 00:46:30,153
Gentlemen?

1291
00:46:30,187 --> 00:46:32,323
-We have to fumigate the
tank, store the toxin.

1292
00:46:32,357 --> 00:46:34,693
-We have to completely
redo the upstairs.

1293
00:46:34,727 --> 00:46:37,095
-Noon tomorrow?

1294
00:46:37,128 --> 00:46:41,633
-Hmm, I was going to
play golf, but no.

1295
00:46:41,667 --> 00:46:43,668
-I know they think
I'm Dennis Weaver.

1296
00:46:43,702 --> 00:46:45,570
You think I'm Dennis
Weaver too, don't you?

1297
00:46:45,603 --> 00:46:46,070
Yes, you do.

1298
00:46:46,103 --> 00:46:46,605
You do.

1299
00:46:48,773 --> 00:46:49,908
-[Singing "the
girl from ipanema"]

1300
00:46:54,478 --> 00:46:57,917
-I hope he owns several
of those shirts.

1301
00:46:57,950 --> 00:47:00,285
-Hello there!

1302
00:47:00,318 --> 00:47:02,053
-I'd like to make a
person-to-person call

1303
00:47:02,087 --> 00:47:06,090
from that one guy
to that other guy.

1304
00:47:06,123 --> 00:47:07,592
-Maybe I should
introduce myself.

1305
00:47:07,625 --> 00:47:08,593
Maybe he'd like me.

1306
00:47:11,162 --> 00:47:13,065
RECEPTIONIST (OFFSCREEN):
Telephone for Colonel Butler.

1307
00:47:13,098 --> 00:47:14,567
Call for Colonel Butler.

1308
00:47:14,600 --> 00:47:15,233
-Or Lovejoy.

1309
00:47:15,267 --> 00:47:16,233
July

1310
00:47:16,267 --> 00:47:20,272
-It's hard to organize a
junta in Vacation Land.

1311
00:47:20,305 --> 00:47:22,707
-Colonel Butler speaking.

1312
00:47:22,740 --> 00:47:24,242
Thank you.

1313
00:47:24,275 --> 00:47:26,143
Give him his binky and
put him in his crib.

1314
00:47:26,177 --> 00:47:27,412
I don't know.

1315
00:47:27,445 --> 00:47:28,447
-There's something else.

1316
00:47:28,480 --> 00:47:29,848
-Nobody quite knows
where they've seen me.

1317
00:47:29,882 --> 00:47:31,917
-Whoever planted that
bug is an amateur.

1318
00:47:31,950 --> 00:47:32,817
-Wrong.

1319
00:47:32,850 --> 00:47:34,218
There's an American
in deep cover

1320
00:47:34,252 --> 00:47:35,387
here, code name Diamond Head.

1321
00:47:35,420 --> 00:47:36,153
And he's good.

1322
00:47:36,187 --> 00:47:37,122
He made it too easy for you.

1323
00:47:37,155 --> 00:47:38,290
-Meaning what?

1324
00:47:38,323 --> 00:47:40,625
-Meaning he expects
you to lead him to me.

1325
00:47:40,658 --> 00:47:42,693
You're being followed.

1326
00:47:42,727 --> 00:47:45,330
First, use Diamond Head's man
and set up in the diving shop.

1327
00:47:45,363 --> 00:47:46,197
Contact our friend.

1328
00:47:46,230 --> 00:47:47,297
-Damn, I'm on speaker phone!

1329
00:47:47,330 --> 00:47:49,300
-Tell him to prepare the
alternate escape route just

1330
00:47:49,333 --> 00:47:49,933
in case.

1331
00:47:49,967 --> 00:47:51,270
We go tomorrow as planned.

1332
00:47:57,375 --> 00:47:58,477
-What about this Diamond Head?

1333
00:47:58,510 --> 00:47:59,645
-He's looking for Tree.

1334
00:47:59,678 --> 00:48:00,878
He'll find him.

1335
00:48:00,912 --> 00:48:01,547
-How?

1336
00:48:01,580 --> 00:48:02,747
That's my job.

1337
00:48:02,780 --> 00:48:04,617
Tell Sakai to call me.

1338
00:48:04,650 --> 00:48:06,250
I'll do the rest.

1339
00:48:06,283 --> 00:48:07,585
-Hold it, turn.

1340
00:48:07,618 --> 00:48:08,087
Beautiful!

1341
00:48:08,120 --> 00:48:10,355
Perfect!

1342
00:48:10,388 --> 00:48:11,355
-Tonight!

1343
00:48:11,388 --> 00:48:13,625
One of these three
contestants will find out

1344
00:48:13,658 --> 00:48:15,027
where they've seen this guy!

1345
00:48:25,670 --> 00:48:26,638
-Tom Jones.

1346
00:48:29,607 --> 00:48:30,107
-Ah!

1347
00:48:30,140 --> 00:48:31,108
Look at that shirt!

1348
00:48:37,982 --> 00:48:39,818
-Move it, Normal Lear.

1349
00:48:39,852 --> 00:48:42,687
-Nickle!

1350
00:48:42,720 --> 00:48:45,090
-Butt-grabbing slacks.

1351
00:48:45,123 --> 00:48:48,027
-When you're proud of
your crack and it shows.

1352
00:48:52,363 --> 00:48:55,933
-Speed, starring Keanu Reeves.

1353
00:48:55,967 --> 00:48:59,337
-The FBI's going to
pay us all to surf?

1354
00:48:59,370 --> 00:49:03,208
-Oh, I better get to the
Banana Splits auditions.

1355
00:49:03,242 --> 00:49:03,742
-Jeanie?

1356
00:49:08,380 --> 00:49:10,915
-Ugh, he would have
to have trifocals.

1357
00:49:10,948 --> 00:49:12,550
-The hair is built into the hat!

1358
00:49:16,087 --> 00:49:17,322
[Phone rings]

1359
00:49:17,355 --> 00:49:18,757
-Aw, it's probably Sherry.

1360
00:49:18,790 --> 00:49:21,493
She probably wants to talk
about the break up again.

1361
00:49:21,527 --> 00:49:25,363
-What can I doodly-do you for?

1362
00:49:25,397 --> 00:49:27,298
-I'll come up.

1363
00:49:27,332 --> 00:49:28,267
-Yes.

1364
00:49:28,300 --> 00:49:30,768
-Jeez, he needs some psst.

1365
00:49:30,802 --> 00:49:31,702
You know.

1366
00:49:31,735 --> 00:49:35,240
-Now where's that
skort outfit I packed?

1367
00:49:35,273 --> 00:49:35,740
-Wow!

1368
00:49:35,773 --> 00:49:37,808
Ooh-wa!

1369
00:49:37,842 --> 00:49:40,778
-You know, I tell you, I
get no respect, no respect.

1370
00:49:40,812 --> 00:49:42,780
-Oh, everybody wants
a piece of Lovejoy.

1371
00:49:47,485 --> 00:49:48,787
-Graeber said you wanted me.

1372
00:49:48,820 --> 00:49:49,688
-In the worst way.

1373
00:49:52,223 --> 00:49:53,558
There's a disco
called The Dragon

1374
00:49:53,592 --> 00:49:55,327
Lady, moored in Honolulu Harbor.

1375
00:49:55,360 --> 00:49:57,928
Be outside on the upper
deck at 2200 hours.

1376
00:49:57,962 --> 00:49:59,330
-Problems?

1377
00:49:59,363 --> 00:50:00,732
-I'll be posing
as that gentlemen.

1378
00:50:00,765 --> 00:50:01,232
-You?

1379
00:50:01,265 --> 00:50:02,633
-Basil Philips.

1380
00:50:02,667 --> 00:50:03,968
Very British, very obvious.

1381
00:50:04,002 --> 00:50:05,403
-Very fey.

1382
00:50:05,437 --> 00:50:07,105
-Oh, Sakai.

1383
00:50:07,138 --> 00:50:09,040
Take a good look.

1384
00:50:09,073 --> 00:50:11,777
I'd hate there to be a case
of mistaken identification.

1385
00:50:14,345 --> 00:50:15,680
-That could be fatal.

1386
00:50:15,713 --> 00:50:17,682
-We're taking a midnight stroll.

1387
00:50:17,715 --> 00:50:18,482
-To Georgia.

1388
00:50:18,515 --> 00:50:19,717
-If my instincts
are correct, I'll

1389
00:50:19,750 --> 00:50:23,655
be having company--
unwelcome company.

1390
00:50:23,688 --> 00:50:25,023
-I understand.

1391
00:50:25,057 --> 00:50:25,957
Oh, and Sakai?

1392
00:50:25,990 --> 00:50:28,527
-Turn down the bed, will you?

1393
00:50:28,560 --> 00:50:29,193
-No marks.

1394
00:50:29,227 --> 00:50:30,662
-No hits, no arrows.

1395
00:50:30,695 --> 00:50:33,732
-Nothing for the authorities.

1396
00:50:33,765 --> 00:50:37,235
-Sakai, if you walk
out that door--

1397
00:50:37,268 --> 00:50:38,737
-He's very raccoon-y.

1398
00:50:41,305 --> 00:50:44,777
-A good thing he uses
smudge-proof eyeliner.

1399
00:50:44,810 --> 00:50:48,113
-Ed Shaughnessy, Hawaiian-style.

1400
00:50:48,147 --> 00:50:51,650
-I'll salute to careful shaving.

1401
00:50:51,683 --> 00:50:54,218
-I don't know what it is or
how it's done, but I like it!

1402
00:50:56,855 --> 00:50:57,988
-San Diego chicken?

1403
00:50:58,022 --> 00:50:59,925
Oh.

1404
00:50:59,958 --> 00:51:00,858
-Hi.

1405
00:51:00,892 --> 00:51:02,760
Here for the Daniel
Inouye fund raiser.

1406
00:51:07,898 --> 00:51:10,368
-He's going to have a Montclaire
moment any minute now.

1407
00:51:13,972 --> 00:51:14,638
Sir?

1408
00:51:14,672 --> 00:51:17,008
Vodka with one ice cube only.

1409
00:51:17,042 --> 00:51:17,775
-You're in luck, buddy.

1410
00:51:17,808 --> 00:51:18,610
We have one.

1411
00:51:21,145 --> 00:51:22,347
-Dear bartender.

1412
00:51:22,380 --> 00:51:22,847
I like you.

1413
00:51:22,880 --> 00:51:23,682
Do you like me?

1414
00:51:23,715 --> 00:51:26,685
Check one.

1415
00:51:26,718 --> 00:51:27,685
-Ooh.

1416
00:51:27,718 --> 00:51:29,687
-Ooh.

1417
00:51:29,720 --> 00:51:30,722
-She's saran-wrapped.

1418
00:51:34,725 --> 00:51:38,663
-Would you give
this to Tso-Tsing.

1419
00:51:38,697 --> 00:51:41,332
-Sure, Mr. Lovejoy!

1420
00:51:41,365 --> 00:51:43,235
-Give everyone an
ice cube, on me!

1421
00:51:45,837 --> 00:51:48,840
-It's All-Annoying
Music Night down here.

1422
00:51:48,873 --> 00:51:52,377
-I hope someone else
is hearing that.

1423
00:51:52,410 --> 00:51:53,745
-Stomp, ladies and gentlemen!

1424
00:51:53,778 --> 00:51:54,278
Stomp.

1425
00:51:57,315 --> 00:51:58,683
Stomp.

1426
00:51:58,717 --> 00:51:59,250
-Pshaw.

1427
00:51:59,283 --> 00:52:00,918
I could have done that.

1428
00:52:00,952 --> 00:52:02,253
-Mr. Phillips?

1429
00:52:02,287 --> 00:52:04,055
You asked to see me.

1430
00:52:04,088 --> 00:52:05,423
-Not wearing that I didn't.

1431
00:52:08,560 --> 00:52:10,828
-Your reputation
doesn't do you justice.

1432
00:52:10,862 --> 00:52:12,063
What's Archer pleasure?

1433
00:52:12,097 --> 00:52:13,765
-My pleasures are personal.

1434
00:52:13,798 --> 00:52:16,067
I never mix them with business.

1435
00:52:16,100 --> 00:52:19,070
-Duty and brains in the
same lovely package.

1436
00:52:19,103 --> 00:52:21,973
You know, your back room's
almost as famous as you are.

1437
00:52:22,007 --> 00:52:24,142
They say luck's a lady.

1438
00:52:24,175 --> 00:52:25,543
-Then she should be courted.

1439
00:52:25,577 --> 00:52:26,077
-Whoa!

1440
00:52:26,110 --> 00:52:28,413
Got a live one here.

1441
00:52:28,447 --> 00:52:29,513
Jackie?

1442
00:52:29,547 --> 00:52:30,082
-(ANNOYED) What?

1443
00:52:33,318 --> 00:52:34,152
There, feel better?

1444
00:52:38,222 --> 00:52:39,223
Be sure to come back.

1445
00:52:39,257 --> 00:52:41,392
I'm freezing you a
special ice cube!

1446
00:52:49,600 --> 00:52:50,067
-Yeah.

1447
00:52:50,100 --> 00:52:51,603
Uh, Northstar Ice?

1448
00:52:51,637 --> 00:52:53,170
Yeah, I need another ice cube.

1449
00:52:53,203 --> 00:52:54,738
Better make it four.

1450
00:52:54,772 --> 00:52:56,842
-Tso-Tsing wants you, pronto.

1451
00:52:56,875 --> 00:52:58,843
Go

1452
00:52:58,877 --> 00:53:01,178
-Ah, go fish.

1453
00:53:01,212 --> 00:53:02,847
-The house shows 10.

1454
00:53:02,880 --> 00:53:04,148
-Play these.

1455
00:53:04,182 --> 00:53:06,283
-Whoa, whoa! [CLEARING THROAT]

1456
00:53:06,317 --> 00:53:07,718
-You seem to do well here.

1457
00:53:07,752 --> 00:53:11,422
-How much is a four
worth, you know?

1458
00:53:11,455 --> 00:53:14,825
-I give my customers what
they want-- the exotic Orient

1459
00:53:14,858 --> 00:53:16,628
and no overcharge.

1460
00:53:16,662 --> 00:53:17,528
-Anything else?

1461
00:53:17,562 --> 00:53:20,132
Information, for example?

1462
00:53:20,165 --> 00:53:21,700
-Information is like sex.

1463
00:53:21,733 --> 00:53:24,568
You can sell it 50 times
and you still own it.

1464
00:53:24,602 --> 00:53:25,403
-Heh, sex.

1465
00:53:25,437 --> 00:53:27,472
-An exchange, then.

1466
00:53:27,505 --> 00:53:29,807
You for Diamond Head.

1467
00:53:29,840 --> 00:53:31,242
-I don't understand.

1468
00:53:31,275 --> 00:53:32,475
Mm, good ice cube.

1469
00:53:32,508 --> 00:53:36,615
-Five years ago, an American
intelligence agent in Bangkok

1470
00:53:36,648 --> 00:53:37,615
lost her cover.

1471
00:53:37,648 --> 00:53:39,083
Her family was
liquidated and she

1472
00:53:39,117 --> 00:53:41,787
was subject to the
usual brainwashing.

1473
00:53:41,820 --> 00:53:44,588
However, her people got her out
and they relocated her here,

1474
00:53:44,622 --> 00:53:47,192
in Hawaii-- naturally,
under an assumed identity.

1475
00:53:47,225 --> 00:53:49,693
-Is this your dessert menu?

1476
00:53:49,727 --> 00:53:51,528
-Tso-Tsing.

1477
00:53:51,562 --> 00:53:53,565
-Birthday prayer for
a special friend.

1478
00:53:53,598 --> 00:53:56,400
Hmm.

1479
00:53:56,433 --> 00:53:57,502
-Kate Jackson!

1480
00:53:57,535 --> 00:54:00,705
Ooh, the smart one.

1481
00:54:00,738 --> 00:54:03,073
-You have a saying--
all Asians look alike.

1482
00:54:03,107 --> 00:54:04,208
-That is so racist!

1483
00:54:04,242 --> 00:54:06,243
I-- oh.

1484
00:54:06,277 --> 00:54:08,112
Well, I wouldn't
bet my life on that.

1485
00:54:08,145 --> 00:54:08,613
-Woo-hoo!

1486
00:54:08,647 --> 00:54:09,513
I mean--

1487
00:54:09,547 --> 00:54:10,515
-There's a contract
out on this girl,

1488
00:54:10,548 --> 00:54:11,917
and there are certain
types here in Honolulu

1489
00:54:11,950 --> 00:54:14,452
who would enjoy collecting you.

1490
00:54:14,485 --> 00:54:16,253
-That's a weird
hat she's got on.

1491
00:54:16,287 --> 00:54:19,057
-Who is Diamond Head?

1492
00:54:19,090 --> 00:54:20,492
-You have made a mistake.

1493
00:54:20,525 --> 00:54:23,695
I do not know Su-La
or Diamond Head.

1494
00:54:23,728 --> 00:54:24,862
-He's got his own airbag.

1495
00:54:28,032 --> 00:54:28,500
-Racko!

1496
00:54:28,533 --> 00:54:31,535
-Pay 20.

1497
00:54:31,568 --> 00:54:32,502
-Tso-Tsing.

1498
00:54:32,535 --> 00:54:34,038
Anyone ever tell you
this is against the law?

1499
00:54:34,072 --> 00:54:35,773
-[COUGHING] Diamond Head!

1500
00:54:35,807 --> 00:54:38,343
[SNEEZING] Diamond Head!

1501
00:54:38,377 --> 00:54:42,180
-Uh, it seems I win.

1502
00:54:42,213 --> 00:54:44,248
-We are playing
for match stakes.

1503
00:54:44,282 --> 00:54:45,050
-Oh, blue tip.

1504
00:54:45,083 --> 00:54:45,883
Strike anywhere.

1505
00:54:45,917 --> 00:54:48,520
-Oh, congratulations.

1506
00:54:48,553 --> 00:54:49,920
-Basil Phillips.

1507
00:54:49,953 --> 00:54:50,688
-Johnny Paul.

1508
00:54:50,722 --> 00:54:51,788
-Friends call me Diamond Head.

1509
00:54:51,822 --> 00:54:54,458
-I should warn you-- Johnny
does this for a living.

1510
00:54:54,492 --> 00:54:55,360
-Oh, that pay good?

1511
00:54:55,393 --> 00:54:58,730
-What, you want
to chase him away?

1512
00:54:58,763 --> 00:55:00,932
-In retrospect, the luggage
seems really fascinating.

1513
00:55:00,965 --> 00:55:01,933
-Oh, yeah.

1514
00:55:04,735 --> 00:55:07,705
-You look like a gambling
man, Mr. Phillips.

1515
00:55:07,738 --> 00:55:09,140
-Well, I, uh-- I take risks.

1516
00:55:09,173 --> 00:55:10,442
-I'm in this movie, aren't I?

1517
00:55:10,475 --> 00:55:16,280
-But only when I know the
odds and the adversary.

1518
00:55:16,313 --> 00:55:19,717
-You make a game of chance
sound like a battlefield.

1519
00:55:19,750 --> 00:55:20,850
-Oh, Lovejoy!

1520
00:55:20,883 --> 00:55:23,020
-When the stakes are high,
that's exactly what it is.

1521
00:55:23,053 --> 00:55:24,888
-The Gospel according
to Napoleon.

1522
00:55:24,922 --> 00:55:26,023
-Spoken like a true fop.

1523
00:55:26,057 --> 00:55:28,427
-Spoken like a military man.

1524
00:55:28,460 --> 00:55:31,128
-I'm lost.

1525
00:55:31,162 --> 00:55:33,932
-Is this an action sequence?

1526
00:55:33,965 --> 00:55:35,467
-Actually, I'm into
the money game.

1527
00:55:35,500 --> 00:55:37,202
You know, real
estate investments,

1528
00:55:37,235 --> 00:55:37,902
that kind of thing.

1529
00:55:37,935 --> 00:55:42,040
-[Blabbering_incoherently]

1530
00:55:42,073 --> 00:55:43,875
-Trying to get a
conversation going.

1531
00:55:43,908 --> 00:55:45,077
-But only when I know the odds.

1532
00:55:49,180 --> 00:55:50,548
-The house shows a queen.

1533
00:55:50,582 --> 00:55:53,083
-Stand.

1534
00:55:53,117 --> 00:55:53,618
-Play these.

1535
00:55:57,522 --> 00:55:57,988
-Blackjack.

1536
00:55:58,022 --> 00:55:59,657
The house wins.

1537
00:55:59,690 --> 00:56:00,125
-Correction.

1538
00:56:02,927 --> 00:56:04,295
You win.

1539
00:56:04,328 --> 00:56:07,098
-(SINGING) Savoir-Faire
is everywhere!

1540
00:56:07,132 --> 00:56:09,067
-It's been a, uh, pleasure Mr.--

1541
00:56:09,100 --> 00:56:09,633
-Paul.

1542
00:56:09,667 --> 00:56:10,635
-Diamond Hea-- uh, Paul.

1543
00:56:10,668 --> 00:56:11,268
-Mr. Paul.

1544
00:56:11,302 --> 00:56:12,637
-Do try the ice cubes.

1545
00:56:12,670 --> 00:56:14,538
If I, uh, hear of
any good investments,

1546
00:56:14,572 --> 00:56:16,207
I'll be sure to look you up.

1547
00:56:16,240 --> 00:56:17,242
-You do that.

1548
00:56:17,275 --> 00:56:21,445
-Is it just me, or
did nothing happen?

1549
00:56:21,478 --> 00:56:22,747
-That's one rotten poker player!

1550
00:56:22,780 --> 00:56:24,048
-He knows who I am.

1551
00:56:24,082 --> 00:56:25,250
And he knows who you are.

1552
00:56:25,283 --> 00:56:27,785
-And he knows who he is.

1553
00:56:27,818 --> 00:56:29,453
-Get Zulu here fast.

1554
00:56:29,487 --> 00:56:32,823
And you stay here,
wait for my call.

1555
00:56:32,857 --> 00:56:36,627
