01:16:11,300 --> 01:16:13,037
-How was your date with Madonna?

2073
01:16:13,070 --> 01:16:13,537
I'm kidding.

2074
01:16:13,570 --> 01:16:15,038
That must hurt.

2075
01:16:15,072 --> 01:16:16,740
-What happened?

2076
01:16:16,773 --> 01:16:17,975
-I forgot to duck.

2077
01:16:18,008 --> 01:16:20,277
-There were at least 20 of
them and they jumped me!

2078
01:16:20,310 --> 01:16:22,145
-You just missed--
a million or two.

2079
01:16:22,178 --> 01:16:22,712
No more.

2080
01:16:25,782 --> 01:16:27,050
-I'm really a singer.

2081
01:16:27,083 --> 01:16:28,885
That's why I'm
tied up like this.

2082
01:16:28,918 --> 01:16:29,987
-Let's tie this guy up.

2083
01:16:30,020 --> 01:16:31,220
Let HPD do the rest.

2084
01:16:31,253 --> 01:16:31,887
Huh?

2085
01:16:31,920 --> 01:16:33,790
-I like to use barbed wire.

2086
01:16:33,823 --> 01:16:34,658
-Yeah, have your fun.

2087
01:16:34,692 --> 01:16:35,758
I'll go capture the terrorists.

2088
01:16:44,233 --> 01:16:45,068
-Hey!

2089
01:16:45,102 --> 01:16:47,537
My friend has a
ring just like that.

2090
01:16:47,570 --> 01:16:49,005
She wants to break up with me.

2091
01:16:51,875 --> 01:16:56,278
-Hey, hey hey, that's
the director's Coke.

2092
01:16:56,312 --> 01:16:57,680
I'll just call her
and find out what

2093
01:16:57,713 --> 01:17:00,683
the whole ring-wax thing means.

2094
01:17:00,717 --> 01:17:01,183
-Hello?

2095
01:17:01,217 --> 01:17:01,818
Steve?

2096
01:17:01,852 --> 01:17:02,485
Roy Thinnes.

2097
01:17:02,518 --> 01:17:03,687
Close off the whole island.

2098
01:17:03,720 --> 01:17:06,923
Aunt Mary, Code Seven, Urgent.

2099
01:17:06,957 --> 01:17:07,423
-Hello dear.

2100
01:17:07,457 --> 01:17:08,357
-Johnny?

2101
01:17:08,390 --> 01:17:11,027
Tree's headed for
Tso-Tsing's trimaran.

2102
01:17:11,060 --> 01:17:12,195
It's The Dragon Lady.

2103
01:17:12,228 --> 01:17:13,930
It's moored in Honolulu Harbor.

2104
01:17:13,963 --> 01:17:14,898
-A sailboat?

2105
01:17:14,932 --> 01:17:16,098
-Sounds fun!

2106
01:17:16,132 --> 01:17:18,168
-He must have friends
waiting for him at sea.

2107
01:17:18,202 --> 01:17:19,602
-Mac, he's got Tso-Tsing.

2108
01:17:19,635 --> 01:17:22,138
-He's got that formula and
we've got to recover it.

2109
01:17:22,172 --> 01:17:24,607
-Mac, I want a shot at him!

2110
01:17:24,640 --> 01:17:25,908
-Tso-Tsing knows the rules.

2111
01:17:25,942 --> 01:17:26,977
-No friends in the house.

2112
01:17:27,010 --> 01:17:28,045
-And so do you.

2113
01:17:28,078 --> 01:17:31,347
I want to stop that
boat at any cost.

2114
01:17:31,380 --> 01:17:32,448
-You owe me.

2115
01:17:32,482 --> 01:17:34,550
-Don't you sass your Aunt Mary!

2116
01:17:34,583 --> 01:17:36,085
-You've got 30 minutes.

2117
01:17:36,118 --> 01:17:39,622
Then I pull the trigger.

2118
01:17:39,655 --> 01:17:42,492
-We've got 30 minutes.

2119
01:17:42,525 --> 01:17:43,693
-Duh duh duh da da!

2120
01:17:43,727 --> 01:17:44,928
Da-- Oh.

2121
01:17:44,962 --> 01:17:46,062
-Jeez, they should
take the boat.

2122
01:17:50,300 --> 01:17:51,902
Boy, you know, I
remember when this aired.

2123
01:17:51,935 --> 01:17:53,970
An entire nation was riveted.

2124
01:17:54,003 --> 01:17:54,970
Everyone was talking about it.

2125
01:17:55,003 --> 01:17:57,340
-Hey, switch on Name of
the Game now, will ya?

2126
01:17:57,373 --> 01:17:59,943
Oh, I forgot, it's
the wrong decade.

2127
01:17:59,977 --> 01:18:01,177
-Hmm?

2128
01:18:01,210 --> 01:18:03,480
-She was going to name
her boat "The Stereotype,"

2129
01:18:03,513 --> 01:18:07,050
but she decided
on "Dragon Lady."

2130
01:18:07,083 --> 01:18:11,253
Tonight's episode--
"No Soup With Buffet!"

2131
01:18:11,287 --> 01:18:13,623
-It's a pity we
haven't met before.

2132
01:18:13,657 --> 01:18:17,560
Espionage is such
a small community.

2133
01:18:17,593 --> 01:18:19,162
It's quite like a
little family, really.

2134
01:18:19,195 --> 01:18:23,167
-In that we all drink
and hurt each other.

2135
01:18:23,200 --> 01:18:25,002
-What's in the bottle?

2136
01:18:25,035 --> 01:18:25,702
-Ah.

2137
01:18:25,735 --> 01:18:27,170
To some, a whirlwind.

2138
01:18:27,203 --> 01:18:31,373
To me, the only reality--
$500,000 in a Swiss bank

2139
01:18:31,407 --> 01:18:31,940
account.

2140
01:18:31,973 --> 01:18:33,075
-I meant the red bottle.

2141
01:18:33,108 --> 01:18:34,410
-Oh, that's Tia Maria.

2142
01:18:34,443 --> 01:18:36,813
-Oh.

2143
01:18:36,847 --> 01:18:38,148
-Is this Hawaii or Seattle?

2144
01:18:41,652 --> 01:18:43,187
-Avast ye-- Oh, forget it.

2145
01:18:43,220 --> 01:18:46,355
-How many people died for
your Swiss bank account?

2146
01:18:46,388 --> 01:18:47,055
-A lot.

2147
01:18:47,088 --> 01:18:49,758
We don't have exact figures yet.

2148
01:18:49,792 --> 01:18:51,762
-Cost of running business?

2149
01:18:51,795 --> 01:18:54,297
That's a price no one can pay.

2150
01:18:54,330 --> 01:18:56,633
Or has the right to.

2151
01:18:56,667 --> 01:18:57,900
-Right?

2152
01:18:57,933 --> 01:18:59,970
You'll be waving the flag next
and George, Queen and country.

2153
01:19:00,003 --> 01:19:00,870
There's no such thing, girl.

2154
01:19:00,903 --> 01:19:02,838
The world is run
by politicians--

2155
01:19:02,872 --> 01:19:03,705
-Oh, boy.

2156
01:19:03,738 --> 01:19:04,975
---demand respectability
without virtue--

2157
01:19:05,008 --> 01:19:06,008
[snoring sounds]

2158
01:19:06,042 --> 01:19:07,377
---pleasure without payment.

2159
01:19:07,410 --> 01:19:08,377
-You without me, sir?

2160
01:19:08,410 --> 01:19:11,347
-And blind men to bury
their honorable dead.

2161
01:19:11,380 --> 01:19:13,683
I just balance the
scales a little.

2162
01:19:13,717 --> 01:19:14,183
-Acting!

2163
01:19:14,217 --> 01:19:15,618
-My way.

2164
01:19:15,652 --> 01:19:18,822
-Even in Hell, you will
balance the scales.

2165
01:19:18,855 --> 01:19:20,590
Right, Mr. Barnaby?

2166
01:19:20,623 --> 01:19:22,125
-I know you are, but what am I?

2167
01:19:22,158 --> 01:19:23,860
-Just steer.

2168
01:19:23,893 --> 01:19:27,997
-I'm sorry, that
was uncalled for.

2169
01:19:28,030 --> 01:19:29,198
-Oh no, Sam Elliott!

2170
01:19:33,437 --> 01:19:37,007
-(SINGING) Please allow
me to introduce myself.

2171
01:19:37,040 --> 01:19:41,243
[Theme music]

2172
01:19:43,880 --> 01:19:44,447
-Herbie!

2173
01:19:44,480 --> 01:19:46,448
What are you doing?

2174
01:19:46,482 --> 01:19:49,552
-Burns and Schreiber
to the rescue!

2175
01:19:49,585 --> 01:19:51,588
-Hah, another member
of his crack team.

2176
01:19:55,792 --> 01:19:57,460
-Hey, TV's Frank
named that boat!

2177
01:20:04,367 --> 01:20:07,537
-He's got a figure
like Marcia Brady!

2178
01:20:07,570 --> 01:20:09,205
-Hey, you should
never run on a dock!

2179
01:20:09,238 --> 01:20:10,940
-Hey, where's my 50 bucks?

2180
01:20:10,973 --> 01:20:12,175
-Don't worry about
it, you'll get it!

2181
01:20:12,208 --> 01:20:15,178
Come on, start her up.

2182
01:20:15,212 --> 01:20:16,680
-Where are we going?

2183
01:20:16,713 --> 01:20:18,582
-Tso-Tsing's trimaran.

2184
01:20:18,615 --> 01:20:20,617
It should be on the
outside, Mamala Bay.

2185
01:20:20,650 --> 01:20:22,518
-What's in it for me?

2186
01:20:22,552 --> 01:20:24,420
-You'll get another 50 bucks!

2187
01:20:24,453 --> 01:20:25,522
Now start it up!

2188
01:20:25,555 --> 01:20:27,490
-Our hero gets
rattled very easily.

2189
01:20:30,393 --> 01:20:31,762
-There's dead involved now.

2190
01:20:31,795 --> 01:20:33,162
The intrigue thickens.

2191
01:20:33,195 --> 01:20:34,497
-I can't look away.

2192
01:20:37,233 --> 01:20:38,000
-That's right.

2193
01:20:38,033 --> 01:20:40,170
A trimaran called
The Dragon Lady.

2194
01:20:40,203 --> 01:20:42,938
She was probably outside
the Kewalo Basin right now.

2195
01:20:42,972 --> 01:20:44,140
-Are we going to overtake?

2196
01:20:44,173 --> 01:20:45,642
-Order him into the wind.

2197
01:20:45,675 --> 01:20:48,612
If he opens fire, respond.

2198
01:20:48,645 --> 01:20:50,547
Stop that boat, no matter what!

2199
01:20:50,580 --> 01:20:51,948
-Yes sir.

2200
01:20:51,982 --> 01:20:53,383
-[GASPS] Jim Henson!

2201
01:20:53,417 --> 01:20:54,183
-On deck.

2202
01:20:54,217 --> 01:20:55,985
Standby to get underway.

2203
01:20:56,018 --> 01:20:57,087
Take in all lines.

2204
01:20:57,120 --> 01:20:57,820
Let's go.

2205
01:20:57,853 --> 01:20:59,020
Priority one.

2206
01:20:59,053 --> 01:21:02,358
-The Coast Guard-- for men
too chicken to join the Navy!

2207
01:21:02,392 --> 01:21:03,360
-Hey!

2208
01:21:03,393 --> 01:21:04,327
God.

2209
01:21:04,360 --> 01:21:06,095
Like I'm going to get
beat up by a sailor.

2210
01:21:13,970 --> 01:21:15,972
-Stay on this course.

2211
01:21:16,005 --> 01:21:17,840
Won't be long.

2212
01:21:17,873 --> 01:21:19,508
-She's been
surreptitiously spreading

2213
01:21:19,542 --> 01:21:20,977
jewelry behind the boat.

2214
01:21:24,847 --> 01:21:28,985
-Derek Jarman's "Blue" had
more action than this movie.

2215
01:21:29,018 --> 01:21:30,753
-What's this all about, Johnny?

2216
01:21:30,787 --> 01:21:32,222
-Where's your flare gun?

2217
01:21:32,255 --> 01:21:34,190
-Here, where I always keep it.

2218
01:21:34,223 --> 01:21:35,192
What do you want it for?

2219
01:21:35,225 --> 01:21:36,225
-What's the range?

2220
01:21:36,258 --> 01:21:38,662
The flare'll burst at 100 yards.

2221
01:21:38,695 --> 01:21:40,363
-How we gonna warn Tso-Tsing?

2222
01:21:40,397 --> 01:21:41,597
-Fly the cocktail flag.

2223
01:21:41,630 --> 01:21:43,700
Nobody ever flies
that going out.

2224
01:21:43,733 --> 01:21:46,068
-I wonder where there's
a saloon in sight?

2225
01:21:46,102 --> 01:21:48,037
[Cheering and laughing]

2226
01:21:48,070 --> 01:21:48,572
-All right.

2227
01:21:52,008 --> 01:21:56,378
-I hear the club's
gotten really exclusive.

2228
01:21:56,412 --> 01:21:59,215
-Stand by for mild
interest on the high seas!

2229
01:22:02,018 --> 01:22:04,220
-Ian McShane in "Lint."

2230
01:22:04,253 --> 01:22:06,757
-I think we've got company.

2231
01:22:06,790 --> 01:22:07,357
-Oh, no.

2232
01:22:07,390 --> 01:22:09,258
Mother!

2233
01:22:09,292 --> 01:22:09,958
-Who is it?

2234
01:22:09,992 --> 01:22:11,728
And I want to know the truth.

2235
01:22:11,762 --> 01:22:13,062
-Hong Kong no good.

2236
01:22:13,095 --> 01:22:14,763
He runs a charter.

2237
01:22:14,797 --> 01:22:16,298
-Gee, your top smells terrific.

2238
01:22:20,337 --> 01:22:24,207
-Aw, they're still
tied to the dock.

2239
01:22:24,240 --> 01:22:24,873
-Let's see.

2240
01:22:24,907 --> 01:22:25,873
Let's see, what else?

2241
01:22:25,907 --> 01:22:28,110
Did I give my corrupt
politician spiel yet?

2242
01:22:37,820 --> 01:22:39,288
-I think Kennedy died.

2243
01:22:42,092 --> 01:22:44,660
-This is like the end of "The
Firm," except it's coherent.

2244
01:22:47,163 --> 01:22:50,233
-Really hair legs
for a-- oh, wow.

2245
01:22:50,267 --> 01:22:52,702
-I'll stay aft.

2246
01:22:52,735 --> 01:22:54,737
-They only get one pass, man.

2247
01:22:54,770 --> 01:22:58,375
-Hey, I've let you down yet.

2248
01:22:58,408 --> 01:23:00,210
-There's a lot of
money here, Mitchell!

2249
01:23:08,818 --> 01:23:12,188
[Goofy chuckling]

2250
01:23:12,222 --> 01:23:13,623
-Yes, I'm that guy!

2251
01:23:13,657 --> 01:23:14,157
Yup.

2252
01:23:19,495 --> 01:23:20,430
-Wow.

2253
01:23:20,463 --> 01:23:22,298
The sail is polyester, too.

2254
01:23:22,332 --> 01:23:22,832
-Wow.

2255
01:23:28,572 --> 01:23:29,105
-Rat patrol!

2256
01:23:29,138 --> 01:23:30,207
That's what you were on.

2257
01:23:34,843 --> 01:23:37,413
-Watch it, Johnny!

2258
01:23:37,447 --> 01:23:38,548
-Watch the shirt jack!

2259
01:23:38,582 --> 01:23:40,450
-Johnny!

2260
01:23:40,483 --> 01:23:41,383
-One excuse, Tree!

2261
01:23:41,417 --> 01:23:41,950
Come on!

2262
01:23:41,983 --> 01:23:43,018
-My mom said I couldn't?

2263
01:23:43,052 --> 01:23:45,722
Dog ate my homework?

2264
01:23:45,755 --> 01:23:47,757
-So he's basically
saying, make my day?

2265
01:23:47,790 --> 01:23:50,193
-Yeah.

2266
01:23:50,227 --> 01:23:53,430
-That was number
one for lost causes.

2267
01:23:53,463 --> 01:23:56,098
-This is such a
satisfying conclusion.

2268
01:23:56,132 --> 01:23:57,900
-This was certainly
worth waiting for, huh?

2269
01:23:57,933 --> 01:24:00,002
-Yeah.

2270
01:24:00,035 --> 01:24:02,638
-Pity we don't have an
apple to put in his mouth!

2271
01:24:02,672 --> 01:24:03,138
Hoh.

2272
01:24:03,172 --> 01:24:05,175
I had that coming.

2273
01:24:05,208 --> 01:24:05,675
-You OK?

2274
01:24:05,708 --> 01:24:08,645
-I am now.

2275
01:24:08,678 --> 01:24:09,578
-Let's do some nitrous!

2276
01:24:12,582 --> 01:24:14,050
-That's the stuff.

2277
01:24:14,083 --> 01:24:15,050
-Bad news, fellas!

2278
01:24:15,083 --> 01:24:16,052
[Sirens]

2279
01:24:16,085 --> 01:24:18,053
-Here comes trouble!

2280
01:24:18,087 --> 01:24:22,058
[Sirens]

2281
01:24:22,092 --> 01:24:24,527
-Either somebody
bursted the law,

2282
01:24:24,560 --> 01:24:26,528
or World War III's just started!

2283
01:24:26,562 --> 01:24:28,532
-It's all right, Hong Kong.

2284
01:24:28,565 --> 01:24:31,000
You just won yourself
a kewpie doll.

2285
01:24:31,033 --> 01:24:34,337
-So the whole point of the
capers was novelty items?

2286
01:24:34,370 --> 01:24:36,672
-I am so glad they got together.

2287
01:24:36,705 --> 01:24:38,942
-Let's switch it over
to Hec Ramsey now.

2288
01:24:38,975 --> 01:24:40,143
-Oh, anything.

2289
01:24:40,177 --> 01:24:41,043
-Epilogue.

2290
01:24:41,077 --> 01:24:42,310
OK, let me guess.

2291
01:24:42,343 --> 01:24:45,682
The last words in this film are
going to be "ah ha ha ha ha."

2292
01:24:45,715 --> 01:24:46,983
-Aw, baby.

2293
01:24:47,017 --> 01:24:49,718
Tu etais incroybable.

2294
01:24:49,752 --> 01:24:51,187
That's French.

2295
01:24:51,220 --> 01:24:52,188
It means you were incredible.

2296
01:24:52,222 --> 01:24:58,127
-[Making_loud_squeaking_noise]

2297
01:24:58,160 --> 01:25:00,497
-You never cease to amaze me.

2298
01:25:00,530 --> 01:25:03,165
-Chevy Chase?

2299
01:25:03,198 --> 01:25:04,533
-I didn't know you could cook.

2300
01:25:04,567 --> 01:25:05,768
-I didn't know you could eat.

2301
01:25:10,807 --> 01:25:12,175
-I'm a maze of hidden talents.

2302
01:25:12,208 --> 01:25:14,610
-Yeah, very well hidden.

2303
01:25:14,643 --> 01:25:18,180
-What about my reward, huh?

2304
01:25:18,213 --> 01:25:20,983
-I do have some
rare Maori carvings.

2305
01:25:21,017 --> 01:25:21,918
-Marijuana carpets?

2306
01:25:26,388 --> 01:25:28,090
-(WITH FRENCH ACCENT) I'm
sorry I'm so fat for you.

2307
01:25:31,393 --> 01:25:32,327
[Phone ringing]

2308
01:25:32,360 --> 01:25:35,030
-[MAKING_GULPING_NOISES]
I have your gum.

2309
01:25:39,502 --> 01:25:40,135
-Hello?

2310
01:25:40,168 --> 01:25:41,537
-Yeah, this is Quinn Martin.

2311
01:25:41,570 --> 01:25:43,505
We're not going to series.

2312
01:25:43,538 --> 01:25:44,807
-Yes.

2313
01:25:44,840 --> 01:25:47,010
Just a minute.

2314
01:25:47,043 --> 01:25:47,943
-Quinn.

2315
01:25:47,977 --> 01:25:48,912
-You.

2316
01:25:48,945 --> 01:25:51,747
And he didn't give his name.

2317
01:25:51,780 --> 01:25:52,782
-I think it's your mother.

2318
01:25:57,753 --> 01:25:58,822
-Johnny?

2319
01:25:58,855 --> 01:25:59,822
-I can see you.

2320
01:25:59,855 --> 01:26:01,157
-I thought you'd like
to know the gold cross

2321
01:26:01,190 --> 01:26:02,558
formant has been destroyed.

2322
01:26:02,592 --> 01:26:03,292
-Click.

2323
01:26:03,325 --> 01:26:04,392
[Imitating dial tone]

2324
01:26:04,425 --> 01:26:05,962
-And the British have passed
extradition on Donovan.

2325
01:26:05,995 --> 01:26:06,862
Yeah!

2326
01:26:06,895 --> 01:26:09,232
Maybe in about, oh, 200 years!

2327
01:26:09,265 --> 01:26:09,798
-Well fine.

2328
01:26:09,832 --> 01:26:11,033
It's over then, right?

2329
01:26:11,067 --> 01:26:12,268
-Oh, this job, yes!

2330
01:26:12,302 --> 01:26:13,468
But there is something else.

2331
01:26:13,502 --> 01:26:15,805
-Not tonight?

2332
01:26:15,838 --> 01:26:18,140
-I'm worried about security
for the Korean ambassador.

2333
01:26:18,173 --> 01:26:18,840
